    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: Discount schedules with gaps between tier ranges (e.g. tier1 ends at 99, tier2 starts at 101).
Why it matters: A quantity falling in the gap (e.g. exactly 100) gets no tier match — CPQ silently applies no discount where the customer expected one. Margin loss when fixed by hand; customer trust loss when caught.
Suppress a finding: when the gap is intentional (the schedule deliberately skips a quantity range).
Disable the detector: only if your tiers are intentionally non-contiguous. Most orgs should leave this on.</value></values>
</CustomMetadata>
